0	163	Helena Dalli (née Abela; born 29 September 1962) is a Maltese politician who served as European Commissioner for Equality from 1 December 2019 to 30 November 2024.
164	203	She is a member of the Labour Party.



203	290	Career


Before politics
Before entering politics, Dalli worked as a model and actress.
291	367	At 17, Dalli won Miss Malta, and represented the country at Miss World 1979.
368	477	She subsequently appeared in the 1985 movie Final Justice as a policewoman who partners with the protagonist.
478	595	After the failure of the film, she left acting and entered politics, working with Labour Party leader Dom Mintoff.



595	766	Parliamentary Secretary
In 1996, Dalli was elected to the Parliament of Malta and appointed Parliamentary Secretary for Women's Rights in the Office of the Prime Minister.
767	895	She was re-elected during the five subsequent elections, making her the second most elected woman in Maltese political history.

895	1171	During her two-year tenure, she put forwards a Childcare Bill to provide for regulations of childcare services both in the public and the private sector, and took care of the drafting of the Gender Eq
1172	1242	Dalli also launched Malta's first white paper on domestic violence.



